T* (            In Chapter 5 of "Born to Run," Bertie faces the heart-wrenching decision of leaving his home for school in) Tj
T* (England and losing his beloved white lion, which is to be sold to a circus. Despite his mother's explanation of the) Tj
T* (necessity of this decision, Bertie feels betrayed. Determined to save his friend, he takes the lion into the wild,) Tj
T* (where he ultimately decides to set him free. In a painful farewell, Bertie shoots over the lion's head to send him) Tj
T* (away, emphasizing themes of love, sacrifice, and the struggle between freedom and captivity.) Tj
